==Token experience==
Some methods, while not being particularly effective sources of Prayer experience in themselves, are useful for other purposes and can provide small amounts of Prayer experience as a byproduct.

===Ruins of Camdozaal===
After completing [[Below Ice Mountain]], the [[Ruins of Camdozaal]] are unlocked, which includes a low-intensity, non-combat (only requires Fishing and Cooking) method of training Prayer.
Using the [[small fishing net]] (in the area, there are spawn points of a small fishing net and a [[knife]], both tools that one will need for this method) and offering all fish types with decent efficiency (tetra stop ruining at Level 61 Cooking), players can obtain experience rates per hour of 5,600 Fishing, 7,400 Cooking, and 2,400 Prayer.
Using the [[big fishing net]] (simplest way to obtain one would be purchasing one for 20 gp from [[Harry's Fishing Shop.]] in [[Catherby]]; players can obtain a knife from the spawn point in the Camdozaal fishing area) and offering all fish types with decent efficiency (catfish stop ruining at Level 78 Cooking), one can obtain experience rates per hour of 7,000 Fishing, 9,100 Cooking, and 3,200 Prayer.

===Cutting sulliusceps===
[[Sulliuscep|Sulliusceps]], an effective method of woodcutting training that does not require tick manipulation, often drop [[unidentified fossils]] upon being cut. These fossils can be redeemed for Prayer experience after calcification at the [[Mycelium pool]] with [[calcite]] and [[pyrophosphite]], providing Prayer experience at approximately a rate of one Prayer experience for every 6 woodcutting experience. Calcite and pyrophosphite can be acquired at the [[Volcanic Mine]], amongst other fossil island activities.

===Hunter's Rumours===
[[Hunter's Rumours]], which unlock [[Quetzal feed]] to finish the [[Quetzal Transport System]], the [[perfected quetzal whistle]], the [[guild hunter outfit]], and [[Quetzin]], provide [[sun-kissed bones]] and [[blessed bone shards]], which can be redeemed at the [[libation bowl]] for Prayer experience. 

===Shades of Mort'ton===
[[Shades of Mort'ton (minigame)|Shades of Mort'ton]], which unlocks among other things [[bloodbark armour]] and [[zealot's robes]], rewards small amounts of Prayer experience when each [[Shade]] is cremated using [[pyre logs]].

=== Vampyre dust and Hallowed Sepulchre ===
After [[Sins of the Father]] is completed, collected [[vampyre dust]] from [[Feral Vampyre|Feral Vampyres]], [[Vampyre Juvenile|Vampyre Juveniles]], or [[Vyrewatch Sentinel|Vyrewatch Sentinels]] can be used in the [[Hallowed Sepulchre]] for a token amount of Prayer experience. Each dust gives 100 Prayer experience when used to open a [[Saradomin Brazier]]. With the [[Hallowed symbol]], you gain 200 Prayer experience per dust.

===Stealing Valuables===
[[Stealing valuables]] for thieving experience has a rare chance of rewarding a [[blessed bone statuette]], which can be broken down into blessed bone shards and sacrificed at the libation bowl for Prayer experience.

===Calcified Rocks===
At {{SCP|Mining|41}} and having started [[Perilous Moons]], [[Calcified rocks]] can be mined for modest AFK [[Mining]] experience and [[blessed bone shards]]. 

===Rogue's Castle chests===
At {{SCP|Thieving|84}} and having completed the [[Hard Wilderness Diary]], the [[Chest_(Rogues' Castle)|chests in the Rogue's Castle]] in the [[Wilderness]] can be stolen from, providing amongst other loot and some of the best [[Thieving]] experience in the game a 1/22 chance of getting 18 [[Vile ashes]]. If offered using [[Demonic offering]], this amounts to a ratio of roughly 1 Prayer experience for every 7.2 thieving experience gained. However, there is a high risk of dying and losing ashes to player killers, so heavy caution is advised. 

